# Organized sandbox for experimenting with reusable level objects.
script power_pulley_panic
# Start beside the fluid tank on the upper catalog floor.
playerStart 1040 260

exit 1485 430 85 220

# Middle deck, with a ladder opening and a two-tile breakable approach to the exit.
solid 0 650 360 24
solid 440 650 880 24
solid 1448 650 124 24

# Bottom foundation. Replacing the old 210-pixel solid foundation with this
# thin floor turns the former black void into a third usable test gallery.
solid 0 868 1600 32
solid 0 0 28 900
solid 1572 0 28 900

# Upper test floor. Its opening lines up with the opening in the middle deck.
solid 28 300 332 24
solid 440 300 1132 24
ladder 376 270 48 598

# Middle-floor display shelves use the otherwise empty vertical space and keep
# the controls, actuators, sensors, and force demonstration visually separated.
platform 50 470 280 14
platform 450 455 350 14
platform 815 555 320 14
platform 1160 620 300 14

# Lightweight fluid test tank on the upper floor.
water 1100 80 400 220 1 0.55 1.0
label 900 20 FLOOR 3 - MOTION AND HAZARDS

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOTTOM GALLERY
# Station 1 (x 28-390): rolling bodies and an inclined surface.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
platform 250 720 118 18
ramp 175 810 240 18 -22
physicsWheel 78 785 24 1.4
boulder 300 685 25 2.6

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Station 2 (x 420-890): pushables, patrol AI, buttons, and balance beams.
# The shelves are aligned; the two see-saws have separate footprints.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
platform 430 700 180 18
platform 690 700 180 18

enemy 545 660 34 40 430 610 80
stoneBlock 465 652 54 48 3.0
stoneBlock 700 760 54 48 3.0
flywheel 825 655 34 4.0 80
steeringWheel 625 630 28 0

button 430 850 62 18
button 820 850 62 18
seeSaw 535 838 210 16 -18 18 7
seeSaw 780 838 210 16 -18 18 7

# Flexible-body samples frame the balance station instead of crossing it.
chain 420 670 420 850 11 1
chain 650 650 650 850 11 1
chain 900 670 900 838 11 1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Station 3 (x 900-1450): separated screw, impact, and trap-door workbenches.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
platform 940 800 200 18
screw 1040 775 150 13 0 210
gear 1000 735 24 1.8
arrowTrap 1130 745 0 -1 1.8 420
platform 1160 780 160 18
boulder 1220 745 28 3.2
trapDoor 1330 838 110 16 0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Middle-right force station: fan response, pinwheel, and rope physics.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fan 1160 570 1 0 250 90 420 1.0
pinwheel 1435 570 24
physicsRope 1140 430 1460 430 370 5 1 1

# Exit approach: projectile lane followed by a breakable floor bridge.
arrowTrap 1480 610 -1 0 1.4 500
breakableTile 1320 650 64 32 2.0
breakableTile 1384 650 64 32 2.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reusable objects from the physics design guide. Motion and hazards occupy the
# upper floor; controls, sensors, and materials are arranged on the middle floor.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Loose rigid bodies.
ball 58 268 14 0.8
barrel 88 256 28 44 1.8
breakableCrate 126 260 40 40 1.2
explosiveBarrel 176 254 30 46 2.0

# Traversal bodies and environment fixtures.
movingPlatform 225 274 72 14 0 -1 86 1.4
elevator 310 274 42 14 0 -1 110 1.0
oneWayPlatform 450 230 92 12
guideRail 552 284 100 12
ceilingHook 475 72 13
fixedJoint 520 72 10
spring 550 76 620 76 7
rod 635 76 710 76 6

# Middle-floor rotating mechanical parts.
label 460 345 FLOOR 2 - MACHINES, CONTROLS, AND FORCES
crank 470 420 20 105
ratchet 520 420 20 90
clutch 570 420 20 100 1
brake 606 402 50 36 0.72
cam 690 420 20 95 8
turntable 745 424 28 70
conveyorBelt 680 632 130 16 55

